WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:06.580
Whitney Pennington Rodgers:
You run the Dubai Future Foundation.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.460
For those of us who are not initiated,
what is a future foundation?

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.940
His Excellency Khalfan Belhoul:
So imagine you run a lab,

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:17.940
and the owner of the lab
comes to you and says,

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:21.380
"You can do whatever you want,

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.460
and you have my full backing

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:29.100
and you have a solid amount
of financial resources.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:33.700
If rules are an issue,
we can change them for you.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:39.900
We can connect you with any relevant
decision maker to break those rules.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.580
We will not be upset if you make mistakes,

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:48.020
and we will support you
on every winning bet you make."

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.820
And in summary, will you take that?

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.220
WPR: I would take that deal.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:56.500
HEKB: OK, so the owner of the lab
is Sheikh Mohammad bin Rashid,

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.060
and the lab is Dubai Future Foundation.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.260
So that’s how it is.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:04.340
We are entitled and empowered
to explore new ideas --

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:06.660
to see where the future is heading.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:11.500
We’ve been supported and backed
by a top board of trustees --

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:13.900
I mean, our chairman is the crown prince.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:19.780
The board members are ministers
and director generals across all sectors.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:22.180
Which means if we want
to disrupt mobility, we can.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:24.580
If we want to talk health tech, we can.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:27.420
If we want to explore fintech, we can.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:31.660
We have the muscle behind us,
and we have the support in case we fail.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:34.820
The unique thing [that] makes us --

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.900
which I’m sure you’re aware of

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:39.660
from the global landscape --

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:42.780
that usually governments
are a hurdle or they take time

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:44.180
or they're bureaucratic.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:47.060
We are hearing from our leaders
that we can actually do this.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.340
This is music to our ears.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:49.540
So this pushes us.

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:53.140
This makes us comfortable
at actually pivoting.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:55.580
And if we have any venture
capitalists out here --

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:57.820
you would understand this
more than anyone.

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:01.420
They don’t talk about [the] 80 percent
of their portfolio that goes bust,

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:03.740
but they really back the winning bets.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:07.420
They’ve all made those mistakes,
but they don’t look at them as mistakes --

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.260
they look at them as learning points.

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:12.220
And I think this mindset
that’s been given to us from leaders,

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:15.980
to really explore and test
and double down on winning bets,

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:18.620
is what makes the Dubai Future
Foundation a success.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:22.380
WPR: I think a lot of nations
and a lot of cities talk about this idea

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:25.700
of progress and being futurist,

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.580
but it's hard to sustain that.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:31.620
What are some of the ways
that you’re able to get buy-in

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:36.300
and to be able to embed in both
government and culture, futurist thinking?

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:39.100
HEKB: What we do
is we start, first of all,

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:42.900
by ensuring that our internal
teams are experts

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:45.820
in understanding where
the future is heading.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:49.060
We invest a lot in people

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:52.860
that have this ... expertise

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.540
when it comes to future foresight.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:58.020
We invest a lot in internal talent.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:03.100
We have a foresight team that does
horizon scanning on a constant basis,

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.620
and this becomes our engine.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:08.060
But we don't stop there because
this is not only confined to us

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:09.380
as Dubai Future Foundation.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:12.660
We also connect with like-minded
networks from all over the world

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.660
that feed us more information.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:19.940
And then this gives us a view
of where the future is heading.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:22.220
And the further you go --
the grayer it becomes.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:25.700
We can maybe have a better prediction
of what’s happening in 2026,

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:27.420
but the more you go,

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:30.740
the more challenging
the guess would be, right?

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.540
But the more conversations you have,

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:35.140
the more inclusion there is
in the conversation,

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:36.940
the better visibility you have.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:41.260
Then it’s all about being agile
and flexible and getting everyone involved

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:43.220
and having the guts to really test.

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:46.940
Test, but at the same time
create a safe environment in testing.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:49.940
So you get the entrepreneurs,
you get the investors,

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:53.060
and you back it up by also
investing as government

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.420
and create an environment --

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:56.700
which is what we call
the sandbox environment --

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:00.300
which is really testing
those ideas in a safe manner.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:03.500
For example, if you're looking
at last-mile drone deliveries,

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:05.020
you're not going to deploy that

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:07.420
before you actually make sure
it's safe for people.

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:09.420
You need that physical space for that.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:12.580
On the less physical
and less tangible kind of projects --

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:15.660
look at the crypto world
and the digital assets --

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:18.940
you don’t see them in front of you,
but the value of them is immense.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:21.140
But can we actually
open them up to the market

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:23.780
before we create a virtual
safe environment,

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:26.180
including all the relevant parties,

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:30.900
to have a proper conversation
on a deployment basis?

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:33.740
I mean, we can do
as much of that as we want,

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:36.420
but if there isn’t a mechanism

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:39.420
of ensuring that this
can be deployed safely

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:42.220
and in a unified way,

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.500
then we'll just be talking to ourselves.

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:48.020
WPR: Well I think Dubai represents
such a compelling example

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:50.060
of economic transformation,

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:51.820
shifting away from oil revenue

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:53.780
to other spaces like tourism.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:58.420
Can you talk about the current
economic state of Dubai

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:02.380
and sort of how you think that will
influence where the city is headed?

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:06.100
HEKB: We are living in a very
turbulent environment.

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:08.980
The Middle East is a very
tough neighborhood.

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:13.460
Our country is not so big
from a size perspective,

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.780
but our ambitions are
bigger than anyone’s.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.820
We have tensions around the world,

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:24.220
whether it’s big nations
conflicting on economicissues,

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:25.620
geopolitical issues,

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:30.780
and the country has pushed itself
to be a bridge of peace, or

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:34.500
when it comes to business,
when it comes to geopolitics.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:38.100
And I think this is what really
attracts people to come to Dubai.

00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:40.220
We as locals

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:44.020
tend to underestimate the safety factor

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:45.540
and the prosperity factor.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:48.020
We just got too comfortable
and got too used to it.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:51.820
But when we have conversations
with our fellow expats

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:55.500
that come in and choose Dubai
or the UAE as home --

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:57.020
we listen to them,

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:58.580
[and it] gives me goosebumps

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:02.980
on how those small details

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:06.460
of safety and prosperity
for them and their families

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:11.220
mean so much that makes us
really appreciate the structure here.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:12.980
But again, we’re not perfect.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:15.020
We've done our fair share of mistakes,

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.900
but we double down on what we do right.

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:22.900
WPR: We seem to be in a very
transformative moment as a world.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:25.740
What role do you think --
when you think about things like,

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:28.540
beyond even just geopolitical
tensions as you mentioned,

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:30.340
and economic issues,

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:32.980
[or] when you think
about existential threats

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:35.900
like climate change or the rise
of artificial intelligence --

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:39.180
what role do you see futurists
thinking playing in global progress?

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:41.140
HEKB: So I’ll tell you my humble advice:

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:44.500
The world has recently
been giving us so many signs,

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:49.500
that there’s
no other way forward

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:52.140
than us to all get together.

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:53.700
You’ve mentioned them.

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:56.220
Geopolitical issues

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.780
are not going to work --

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:00.380
we need to work together for peace.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:04.380
[The] digital economy,
which is in trillions of dollars

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:07.620
when we talk about the value of AI,

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.860
we’re talking, economy-wise,

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:11.500
about trillions --

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:12.780
that’s another sign.

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.940
Climate change,

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:16.460
how can we solve for that?

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:19.540
There needs to be, we've seen it
in COP announcements and beyond,

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:22.220
there needs to be unity.

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:24.980
AI.

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:26.580
I mean,

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:28.620
if I start to talk about AI, I won't stop.

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:29.940
I mean, how many of us ...

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:31.460
Let me maybe start with you.

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:36.900
How much do you use ChatGPT,
Grok, or you name it, those LLMs?

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:38.060
Do you use it?

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.260
WPR: Regularly.

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:40.700
HEKB: Do you use it daily?

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:41.900
WPR: Probably, yeah.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:43.100
HEKB: I use it daily.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:44.260
Raise of hands.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:45.460
Do you use it daily?

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:46.660
OK.

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:49.060
Do you use it to the extent
that you actually feel

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:51.780
there's a person sitting
on the other side talking to you?

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.580
WPR: Not yet, but I know many who do.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:55.260
HEKB: I'm close to that.

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:58.340
I’m telling you --
from the fact that we interact

00:07:58.340 --> 00:08:00.460
and the emotional angle sometimes you get,

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:02.220
and the responses --

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:06.220
we haven’t even scratched the surface
on how [to] deal with that.

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:09.580
And you feel so comfortable talking
to ChatGPT and many of those LLMs,

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:12.020
so imagine you actually --

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:13.500
this gets,

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:17.460
and I’ve said this, maybe I might sound
like a broken record to my colleagues --

00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:22.260
but imagine having this conversation
with a robot that looks like a human --

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:24.860
which we are not far from seeing,

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.580
and I promise you that
this is going to come very soon --

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:30.180
with the same intellect of the ChatGPT,

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:32.820
[or] even a thousand times
much more than that.

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:37.260
What happens to humanity
and how do we really interact,

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:39.380
even from an emotional standpoint?

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:42.620
We have some weak and vulnerable
individuals around the world

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.260
that feel more comfortable
with robots than humans.

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:48.540
So what would this mean to us as humanity?

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.900
Are we going to get attached to robots?

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:52.580
How are we going to regulate that?

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:56.420
How are we going to really extract value
[from] artificial intelligence?

00:08:56.460 --> 00:09:00.780
That’s why I’m saying [that]
what we see with ChatGPT now

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:03.380
is the first second of the first minute

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:06.100
of the first hour of the first day

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:11.220
of the first year of this beast
that has so much value,

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:14.940
but that we really need to embrace [it],
and we need to embrace [it] jointly.

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:18.260
And there's no chance
that Dubai or the UAE

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:20.020
or the Middle East can do it alone.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:21.860
Nor the US, nor China --

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:24.660
it’s a collaborative effort.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.940
Even look at our kids now [and]

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:29.220
their attachment to technology --

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:30.500
what is the right balance?

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.220
They’re so smart in front of screens,

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:36.420
but if you ask them to come on stage
and have a conversation,

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:37.980
they might not be as comfortable

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:40.380
because they’re just
so involved with technology,

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:43.140
and they do things that I’ll probably
never think of doing

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:46.860
because they’re so into it,
and they’re doing such an amazing job.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:50.020
But life is not only about that --
it’s how you strike the balance.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:52.460
And how do we really
huddle up together as humanity?

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:56.580
Because technology is super valuable,
but humans are more important.

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:58.660
WPR: Well, Your Excellency,

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:01.380
I cannot let you go without
asking you this last question.

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:03.740
You spend so much time
thinking about the future.

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:06.660
What do you think is the big thing
that many of us are missing

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:08.340
when we think about what's ahead?

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:10.300
HEKB: There's one that sticks out to me.

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:12.980
So I'll mention a few and then
I'll tell you which one.

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:16.580
So I mean, longevity and living to --

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:18.420
especially with the ...

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:20.860
advancement of neuroscience
at the moment --

00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:23.220
we can see people living until 150 years,

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:24.660
and this is not far from now.

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:28.900
I think [this is] a statement
that is exciting to many.

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:32.340
I’m not sure if you guys are excited
about this, but [for] many people --

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:33.740
if you’re in good health --

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:35.700
would want to live to 150.

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:37.540
I think this is not far off,

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:42.820
given the advancement
of genetics and DNA sampling.

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:45.420
And like I said, neuroscience.

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:50.220
I think humans, being
a multi-planetary species,

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:52.020
are not far from that as well.

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:54.980
The access to different planets
has become easier and easier

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:56.540
and cost-effective.

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:59.540
So this is also a bold kind of thought

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:03.420
that’s probably exciting scientists.

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:06.020
... I think we have enough on Earth.

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:08.820
I don't know if we want to be there,
but of course, I mean,

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:13.020
having that is something
that everyone is excited about.

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:15.020
It’s a bold statement but achievable.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:19.060
But the one that really, really,
really makes me think a lot,

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:21.100
[and] is slightly relevant to the comment

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:22.500
I mentioned, is:

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:28.700
once you really infuse human intelligence

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:31.180
with artificial intelligence

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:33.220
into one neural network,

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:36.020
when this happens,

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:39.300
this is when things
are going to be really exciting

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:43.460
because we're talking
about AI being super smart,

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:45.460
almost human-like.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.340
And this, to the previous point,

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:50.740
is happening and happening very soon.

00:11:50.780 --> 00:11:52.660
Look at how we're dealing with ChatGPT.

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:56.060
But then what if AI was
infused in a human,

00:11:56.060 --> 00:12:00.780
having a single kind of network

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:04.260
... that connects human intelligence

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:05.940
with artificial intelligence?

00:12:05.940 --> 00:12:08.380
I think, with neuroscience,
this is not very far.

00:12:08.380 --> 00:12:13.820
And this is something that really
requires, again, collaboration,

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:17.740
understanding and unity,
because this is a whole new world.

00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:21.260
WPR: Well, Your Excellency,
this has been insightful and exciting.

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:22.980
I'm sure I speak for everyone here.

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:25.700
Thank you so much for taking
the time to be with us today.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:28.020
(Applause)

